        "x1": 0.8227873160169016,
        "y1": 0.38060641047930477
      },
      "text": "D is a secure dominating set of G if and only if every vertex in V (G) \\ D is D-defended.",
      "html": null,
      "level": null,
      "section_hierarchy": []
    },
    {
      "block_type": "text",
      "box": {
        "page": 0,
        "x0": 0.8329478743808721,
        "y0": 0.36683229484943425,
        "x1": 0.8939283782360601,
        "y1": 0.38060641047930477
      },
      "text": "We also",
      "html": null,
      "level": null,
      "section_hierarchy": []
    },
    {
      "block_type": "text",
      "box": {
        "page": 0,
        "x0": 0.11765199549057904,
        "y0": 0.38562029539936715,
        "x1": 0.8941209581163194,
        "y1": 0.3993944110292377
      },
      "text": "note that if D is a dominating set of G and epn(u, D) = ∅ for some u ∈ D, then every neighbor of u",
      "html": null,
      "level": null,
      "section_hierarchy": []
    },
    {
      "block_type": "text",
      "box": {
        "page": 0,
        "x0": 0.11765199549057904,
        "y0": 0.40440829594930017,
        "x1": 0.7337298424415339,
        "y1": 0.4181824115791706
      },
      "text": "in V (G) \\ D is D-defended by u. We state this observation formally as follows.",
      "html": null,
      "level": null,
      "section_hierarchy": []
    },
    {
      "block_type": "text",
      "box": {
        "page": 0,
        "x0": 0.11765204535590278,
        "y0": 0.4322872210030604,
        "x1": 0.8941228529986214,
        "y1": 0.4460613366329309
      },
      "text": "Observation 2. If D is a dominating set of a graph G and epn(u, D) = ∅ for some vertex u ∈ D,",
      "html": null,
      "level": null,
      "section_hierarchy": []
    },
    {
      "block_type": "text",
      "box": {
        "page": 0,
        "x0": 0.11765064912683823,
        "y0": 0.45107472063315035,
        "x1": 0.6654916900435305,
        "y1": 0.46484883626302087
      },
      "text": "then every neighbor of u that belongs to V (G) \\ D is D-defended by u.",
      "html": null,
      "level": null,
      "section_hierarchy": []
    },
    {
      "block_type": "text",
      "box": {
        "page": 0,
        "x0": 0.1354933096692453,
        "y0": 0.48395375049475464,
        "x1": 0.8939219954746221,
        "y1": 0.49772786612462516
      },
      "text": "As a consequence of Observation 2, if D is a dominating set of G and epn(u, D) = ∅ for every",
      "html": null,
      "level": null,
      "section_hierarchy": []
    },
    {
      "block_type": "text",
      "box": {
        "page": 0,
        "x0": 0.11764765720741421,
        "y0": 0.5027411730602533,
        "x1": 0.8941181656581904,
        "y1": 0.5165152886901239
      },
      "text": "u ∈ D, then every vertex in V (G) \\ D is D-defended, implying that D is a secure dominating set of",
      "html": null,
      "level": null,
      "section_hierarchy": []
    },
    {
      "block_type": "text",
